<h2>India's fastest, simplest export lane</h2>
<p>Nepal is unlike every other market on this site in one important way: there's no ocean freight involved. Goods move overland from northern India through established border crossings, often reaching Nepali buyers in a matter of days rather than weeks. Combined with the wide acceptance of Indian Rupees in Nepal, the trade-finance and logistics friction on this lane is lower than almost anywhere else we ship.</p>

<h2>What that means practically</h2>
<p>If you're sourcing product for delivery in Nepal, ask us whether it can be routed from a northern Indian sourcing point rather than assuming a standard port-based logistics chain. For maize, spices and similar staples, this can mean substantially shorter lead times than our sea-freight markets.</p>

<h2>The India–Nepal Trade Treaty</h2>
<p>Many goods traded between the two countries benefit from preferential access under the bilateral trade treaty. We provide the origin documentation required to support a treaty claim — your customs agent on the Nepal side can confirm which products qualify and the specific paperwork needed.</p>

